Loud, always-on (not DEBUG-gated) warning logged whenever a request's KV
cache is being freed and some or all of it was never offloaded -- i.e.
it's gone for good and continuing that conversation will need a full
recompute rather than a cache lookup. Fires in two cases:

  - No KV-offloading connector configured at all: every freed block is
    unconditionally gone, so this fires for any request with computed
    tokens.
  - An offloading connector (e.g. OffloadingConnector) is configured but
    some tail of the request's content was never queued for store, past
    a one-chunk margin (a normal finish queues its trailing chunk's
    store job on the *next* schedule step -- request_finished()'s own
    docstring -- so a small, safe lag right at completion is expected
    and shouldn't be noise on every routine request).

Verified quiet through normal offloaded completions (only firing on the
genuine sub-chunk tail lag, not spuriously on every request), and
correctly loud with no connector configured. See
docs/mamba-align-prefill-leak.md for the unrelated-but-nearby investigation
this came out of.

